prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle of the county&rsquo;s grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those 75 years. In 2025, February to March came in at 30% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, March to April sits at 175% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 2011, and grid 14520 got 39% of normal that year.</p>"}
